{
    "chapter_num": 1,
    "verses_count": 22,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Elimelech’s Family Goes to Moab"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now it came to pass, in the days when the judges "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. judged"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "ruled, that there was a famine in the land. And a certain man of Bethlehem, Judah, went to "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "As a resident alien"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "dwell in the country of Moab, he and his wife and his two sons. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The name of the man "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Elimelech, the name of his wife "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Naomi, and the names of his two sons "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Mahlon and Chilion—Ephrathites of Bethlehem, Judah. And they went to the country of Moab and remained there. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Elimelech, Naomi’s husband, died; and she was left, and her two sons. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now they took wives of the women of Moab: the name of the one "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Orpah, and the name of the other Ruth. And they "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "lived"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "dwelt there about ten years. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then both Mahlon and Chilion also died; so the woman survived her two sons and her husband."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Naomi Returns with Ruth"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then she arose with her daughters-in-law that she might return from the country of Moab, for she had heard in the country of Moab that the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " had visited"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "attended to"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " His people by giving them bread. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Therefore she went out from the place where she was, and her two daughters-in-law with her; and they went on the way to return to the land of Judah. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Naomi said to her two daughters-in-law, “Go, return each to her mother’s house. The "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " deal kindly with you, as you have dealt with the dead and with me. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " grant that you may find rest, each in the house of her husband.”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So she kissed them, and they lifted up their voices and wept. "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they said to her, “Surely we will return with you to your people.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Naomi said, “Turn back, my daughters; why will you go with me? "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "Are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " there still sons in my womb, that they may be your husbands? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Turn back, my daughters, go—for I am too old to have a husband. If I should say I have hope, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "if"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " I should have a husband tonight and should also bear sons, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "would you wait for them till they were grown? Would you restrain yourselves from having husbands? No, my daughters; for it grieves me very much for your sakes that the hand of the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " has gone out against me!”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then they lifted up their voices and wept again; and Orpah kissed her mother-in-law, but Ruth clung to her."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And she said, “Look, your sister-in-law has gone back to her people and to her gods; return after your sister-in-law.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Ruth said:"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Entreat"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Urge me not"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " me not to leave you,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "Or to"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " turn back from following after you;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For wherever you go, I will go;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And wherever you lodge, I will lodge;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Your people "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "shall be"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " my people,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And your God, my God."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Where you die, I will die,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And there will I be buried."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " do so to me, and more also,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "If "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "anything but"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " death parts you and me.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When she saw that she "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. made herself strong to go"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "was determined to go with her, she stopped speaking to her."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now the two of them went until they came to Bethlehem. And it happened, when they had come to Bethlehem, that all the city was excited because of them; and the women said, “"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "Is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " this Naomi?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But she said to them, “Do not call me "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Pleasant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Naomi; call me "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Bitter"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Mara, for the Almighty has dealt very bitterly with me. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "I went out full, and the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " has brought me home again empty. Why do you call me Naomi, since the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " has testified against me, and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb. Shaddai"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "the Almighty has afflicted me?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So Naomi returned, and Ruth the Moabitess her daughter-in-law with her, who returned from the country of Moab. Now they came to Bethlehem at the beginning of barley harvest."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}